e more open discussion, but the old Lemurian standard remains. The Lemurian etiquette was that Transgressions were an often necessary but rather impolite part of life, and an embarrassing sign of losing control at worst. Remember, the Lemurians are fighting a battle with reality, and they expect members to fight wisely. Going overboard with Transgressions is like charging a trench naked. <br /> <br /> And I've been thinking about how to keep the players together. Basically, Isolation is a semi-theme. Isolation is a form of transgression: we're group animals, after all. Mages feel Isolation in their own awful way: each Mage is stuck on the island of their Paradigm, burdened by a view of an ideal universe they can never quite articulate to others. And this is why they form groups. Paradoxically (and paradoxes are another major theme), it's this isolation and individualism that makes Mages stick together. After all, no one else truly understands your Paradigm, but other Mages come close. Some of them even share it with only minor differences. Social connection also helps with Wisdom loss and avoiding becoming Unmada: that's why Mages have Touchstones. Now, socializing with regular humans is best for this, but socializing with other Mages helps a lot. The Peerage and Lemuria realize. The Peerage has it as part of their ideology, while Lemuria grudgingly realized that Mages who go off alone in volcano lairs and never come to meetings tend to be much likelier to bring their careers to an early, and often explosive and/or radioactive end, which does not help The Serpent at all. This is why the cabal structure was created: the idea of small groups of mages forming, taking on a particular territory or area of study or task, and building a shared mythology and a clublike structure around their Paradigms is an excellent way to stabilize and alleviate some of the burdens of Magehood. The Peerage pushes the cabal ideal most strongly, while Lemurian cabals tend to be looser-knit. Some gently guide new Mages to form cabals, while others bluntly say &quot;if you don't want to blow up, find some friends&quot;. <br /> <br /> Overall, this means that more-stable and more-playable Mages tend to cluster in small groups, while less-stable Mages tend to be hermits or leaders of large groups of minions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:06:44-07:00","id":966549,"title":"","content":"Trying to do two things at once was getting me nowhere, so I've decided to switch my focus entirely to The Lightning Chronicle, because that's the one that's most urgently needed. I've been doing a lot of thinking and reflecting, and I'm realizing that I'd almost rather Mage didn't exist at all instead of existing in a different form. Sorcerers and mad scientists are best handled as minor templates (though I'd love more support for these) to stay true to the themes of the setting, and Deviant has the rest covered. I'm still going to try to finish this eventually, however, because there was so much I loved in Ascension and Genius and I don't want to lose it. Also, replacing Mage is probably much easier than removing it. At least this way, I can more easily fix up existing Mage-related crossover content. But TLC is definitely the greater priority. Promethean really desperately needs it, so I'm switching focus to that. Plus, I'm a lazy bastard and it's the easier of the two projects. <br /> <br /> Look, let's be honest. No one is going to read either of these even if I finish them. The fact that I'm still working on them is probably a bad sign, and I should probably just let go. Let go as in leave the fandom entirely. I can make all the homebrew I want, but that won't make things right. It'll still sting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T16:33:46-07:00","id":969522,"title":"","content":"Okay, news again. I'm still focusing on The Lightning Chronicle right now, but the question of whether or not to continue this is a bit less clear. It was some threads about the &quot;but why isn't there a heroic splat&quot; that made me think of it. No, I'm not intending Mages to become that: they're already too much like superheroes for me. It's that I realized there's still a niche for a game primarily about what happens when you try to change the world. None of the other games have that as a primary: they mostly concern beings who did not choose their supernatural status but had it thrust upon them, and their conflicts are mostly driven by survival and reaction. Also, I want an entirely selfmade splat- no one can force you to Catalyze. Those two work well together: trying to change the world and being responsible for what you are both make for excellent personal horror in ways that none of the lines really explore. Minor templates explore it amazingly well, though, so I'm also making sure to have a lot that differentiates Mages from minor templates- not just &quot;mages are way better and stronger and know more.&quot; Reasons why someone would choose to be a minor template and not a Mage. <br /> <br /> I've been too hard on Awakening, and since it wasn't what I wanted I ended up resenting it more and more until I was just lashing out at it, ignoring its merits. So I'm not sure if I want a totally new game or an Awakening hack. I admit that Awakening fits that niche, it just doesn't fit it in the way I'd prefer. <br /> <br /> To summarize:<br /> \u2022 No mad science options automatically makes me predisposed against something. Plus, mad scientists deserve a major template. <br /> \u2022 The paths are waaaaaaay to restrictive for a game about changing the world with the power of your will. <br /> \u2022 Not enough focus on mages as monsters. <br /> \u2022 Mages are way too powerful and Mage supremacy is still too much of a threat. <br /> \u2022 Simultaneously too many and not enough possibilities. Magic doesn't feel dark and dangerous and self-destructive. <br /> \u2022 The Astral is cool, but Bardos and Manes were cooler. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking of adding a new aspect to Mages to focus on what makes their condition a curse: The Light. The light is the inner fire that powers Mages- not just magical energy, but their connection to their Paradigm and Catalyst. The Light makes demands of Mages: I'm thinking they risk willpower loss, power loss, derangements, or other things if they go a certain amount of time without expressing their a Paradigm: using magic, working on a project, completing an Oblation. I really want being a Mage to feel like a curse, and Awakening just doesn't do that for me. Most Mages wouldn't want to go back to being human, and that means they aren't monstrous enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:17:45-07:00","id":970213,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering, is there anyone who's really interested in this or has any ideas? I'm making it a secondary priority, but I still want to do it eventually, because I've been trying to like Awakening and I still can't help but think it could be so much better. <br /> <br /> I actually have a fair bit done- I finally got over the hump of working out how spellcasting actually works, I have the setting fully described, I have merits, and so on. <br /> <br /> The style merits I had planned would probably be good as Guide content. I'm waiting to release the guide until after Dark Eras 2 and the Crossover Chronicle are out, so I can use those to include eras and crossover info rewritten for the new setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:08:44-07:00","id":970261,"title":"","content":"I'm somewhat interested in how this will all turn out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:10:12-07:00","id":970319,"title":"","content":"Which parts are most interesting, out of curiosity? And do you have any feedback? Suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:03:09-07:00","id":970486,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking I might have to go ahead with this. I've been trying to like Awakening, trying to make it work, but it's just not working out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:42:12-07:00","id":970507,"title":"","content":"I might make a &quot;1001 Workings&quot; thread before the final release as soon as the rules for Workings are formalized and posted, so I can test out the system and see what people think of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:52:00-07:00","id":970513,"title":"","content":"I'm keeping in mind what arc and Hayley told me about emphasizing the theme of transgression in design and having everything reinforce it. That's why I made Transgression Actions part of spellcasting, and why I renamed them from Reach. <br /> <br /> Transgression is, after all, the key to all of this. It's why I have to do this. It's why it can't just be a hack of Mage or Genius. Because there's a hole that needs to be filled, and Transgression is what fills it. ChroD is about playing a monster and exploring horror archetypes. Mages in Awakening are not monsters or horror archetypes. When magic-users show up in horror fiction, they are nothing like Awakening Mages. In fact, they occupy the same conceptual space as mad scientists- though mad scientists are much more prevalent and popular. The mage-as-monster and the mad scientist are defined by transgression. That's what makes them monsters. This &quot;knowing the secrets of the universe that the normies don't know&quot; doesn't make a monster. Awakening is an urban fantasy game. It's a dark occult superhero game. But it is not a personal horror game about exploring a horror archetype. That is the hole Transgression fills. <br /> <br /> Back on topic, the idea of transgression led me to incorporate it into the guidelines for Oblations and Paradigms: both need to be transgressive in some way. An Oblation has to at least be something most people would think was weird if they saw you doing it. You are channeling the energy of rebellion into a shovel and using it to scrape bits of raw energy off the walls of the universe. <br /> <br /> Paradigms must also be transgressive. They must in some fundamental way go against the &quot;paradigm&quot; that the character exists in. So the luminiferous aether couldn't become the basis for a Paradigm until after it was disproven. That means that someone who is a member of an existing supernatural organization (mystery cult, conspiracy, etc) can only Catalyze if they have a Paradigm that violates their group's understanding of the world. So, a member of a God-Machine cult could not Catalyze with the Machine as it is as her Paradigm. She could, however, Catalyze with the Paradigm of &quot;the true consciousness of the machine is sleeping within it and I can manipulate it using radio waves, by doing this I can awaken it and usher in a new golden age&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T15:56:09-07:00","id":970953,"title":"","content":"Been doing some more thinking. Not just trying to like Awakening, but trying to look at things without the prejudice of built up from all the pointless angry arguments I've started about it. <br /> <br /> And, surprisingly, I still want to do this. Because I've taken an honest, deep look at Awakening, and I've realized that it's a perfectly fine urban fantasy/superhero game with a lot that I actually like. It just doesn't fit in ChroD. That's one of the reasons I'm deliberately making this project as crossover friendly as possible: because it's something meant directly for fans of the other lines. <br /> <br /> Another possible thread: something in the Hunter forum about how Hunters interact with the Inspired. It'll probably be easier than Hunter vs. Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:18:04-07:00","id":971046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933738-mage-the-transgression-dev-thread?p=970953#post970953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just doesn't fit in ChroD.</div> </div> </div> </div>-Geckopirateship said, realizing only a moment later that he was talking about Mage. Then he laughed.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, I'm pretty uninterested in this thing myself, as I like Mage and I don't like Genius, but I hope you enjoy doing this, and I hope you will end with a product you can use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T23:23:46-07:00","id":978885,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Removed pointless exaggerated display of woe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-30-2016, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}